    "title": "Siro's Cup fundraiser marks 32 years aiding disability services - NewsBreak",
    "text": "SARATOGA SPRINGS, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — The unofficial kickoff to the Saratoga racing season drew a crowd to Siro’s Restaurant on Wednesday for a good cause. The 32nd annual Siro’s Cup fundraiser helps the Center for Disability Services provide a wide range of services for children and adults. While the party draws hundreds of people, and the silent auction gets even more attention online, the very first Siro’s Cup was very different. “Thirty-three years ago, myself and a group of community leaders met at the University Club in downtown Albany. Davis Mead, who was an owner here at Siro’s, was with us,” Anne Schneider Costigan with the Center for Disability Services recounted. “And we were talking about what goes on at the Saratoga racing season and what we could do. There were all these parties, and Davis turns to us and says, ‘But there’s nothing the eve of opening day,’ and that’s when all this started.” The first year had about 200 people in attendance and raised over $13,000. Schneider Costigan said it’s only grown from there. Read the latest from NEWS10: NEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader! For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
